course: dictionary
lesson: 2553
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «In hot weather children can become dehydrated quickly, with headache, tiredness and dizziness as the first signs.» The clues are headache and dizziness, so dehydrated means a body has lost too much water.
explain: Dehydrated can also describe food. Dried food has had its water taken out, so it lasts longer. If the sentence is about soup, fruit or camping meals, dehydrated probably means dried, not thirsty.
explain: Footy players sometimes joke, «I'm so dehydrated after footy.» This is informal: the speaker means they are very thirsty, not that their body is in danger. Ask which meaning fits the clues before you choose.
fact: Dehydrated means having lost too much water from the body.
fact: Dehydrated can also describe food that has had its water removed, such as dehydrated fruit or dehydrated soup.
fact: «Get dehydrated» and «become dehydrated» are common phrases, and «severely dehydrated» means very badly dehydrated.
fact: Signs of dehydration include thirst, tiredness, dizziness and a headache.
fact: If you feel dehydrated, stop, sit in the shade, drink water and tell an adult.
exercise: «In hot weather children can become dehydrated quickly.» What are the first signs to watch for? | Hiccups and a long sleep | Sunburn and a sore nose | *Headache, tiredness and dizziness | Bright new shoes
exercise: Camping food is often dehydrated. What does dehydrated mean for food? | Frozen solid | Cooked in a pan | *Dried, with the water taken out | Covered in sugar
exercise: «I'm so dehydrated after footy.» What is the joke saying? | Covered in mud | *Very thirsty | Hurt in a tackle | Tired of playing games
test: Why do scientists dehydrate food? | To make it heavier | *To remove water so bacteria cannot grow | To make it change colour | To make it grow faster
test: Which sentence uses dehydrated to mean the body has lost too much water? | *"Sam had a headache and felt dizzy because he was dehydrated after the hot day" | "The dehydrated soup needs hot water" | "Dehydrated fruit is sweet and chewy" | "Our dehydrated meals are in the bag"
exam: Ben reads, «Dehydrated food lasts longer on the trail.» What does dehydrated mean here? | Very angry | Covered in ice | *Dried, with the water taken out | Lost too much water from the body
